{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:fb61f4510d65d959","name":"Kel Dor","source":{"id":"source:reference-fb61f4510d65d959","title":"Kel Dor","revision":26685,"timestamp":"2025-05-30T04:19:36Z","sha256":"75075081701ea367c28974423949cd87e46c1808d4854d2e3cb2dd81f9a9c4a7","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=26685","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Kel%20Dor&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-fb61f4510d65d959","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Core Rulebook"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Core_Rulebook"}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["The Kel Dor evolved on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dorin"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dorin","referenceId":"reference:4331a79784e79b6d"},", a world with an atmosphere consisting mostly of helium and a gas that is unique to that world. As such, Kel Dor cannot breathe on planets with common nitrogen/oxygen atmospheres. Conversely, Dorin's atmosphere is toxic to most nonnative life.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["On other planets, Kel Dor dwellings provide their native atmosphere (stored in large tanks). When outside, Kel Dor must wear breath masks and goggles. They can neither see nor breathe without these devices. Most Kel Dor breath masks include vocoders that amplify the wearer's speech; while their vocal cords function normally in their native atmosphere, Kel Dor must shout to provide sound in other environments. Their eyesight however, is enhanced when they are away from ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dorin"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dorin","referenceId":"reference:4331a79784e79b6d"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Kel Dor Characteristics"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Personality:"]}," Calm and kind, the Kel Dor never turn away a being in need. Still, most believe in quick, simple justice (even engaging in vigilantism).\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Physical Description:"]}," The average Kel Dor stands between 1.6 and 2 meters tall and weighs 70 kilograms. Their skin ranges from peach to deep red, and most have black eyes.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Age Groups"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Age_Groups"},":"]}," Kel Dor age at the following stages:\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"table","children":["\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["CHILD\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["YOUNG ADULT\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["ADULT\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["MIDDLE AGE\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["OLD\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["VENERABLE\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["1-11 Years\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["12-15 Years\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["16-44 Years\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["45-59 Years\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["60-69 Years\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["70+ Years\n"]}]}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Homeworld:"]}," The technological planet of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dorin"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dorin","referenceId":"reference:4331a79784e79b6d"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Languages:"]}," The Kel Dor can speak, read, and write both Basic and Kel Dor.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Example Names:"]}," Dorn Tlo, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Plo Koon"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Plo_Koon","referenceId":"reference:9248b42c377ab418"},", Torin Dol.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Adventurers:"]}," Kel Dor commonly become diplomats (",{"tag":"a","children":["Nobles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nobles"},"), bounty hunters (",{"tag":"a","children":["Scouts"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scouts"},"), and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi","referenceId":"reference:0b0e48747027a29d"},". Given their altruism and sense of justice, many enter law enforcement.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Kel Dor Species Traits"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Kel Dor share the following Species Traits:\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Ability Modifiers:"]}," All Kel Dor receive a +2 bonus to both their ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dexterity"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dexterity"}," and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Wisdom"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Wisdom"},", but suffer a -2 penalty to their ",{"tag":"a","children":["Constitution"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Constitution"},". Kel Dor are quick and wise, but they suffer from weaker constitutions than others."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Medium Size:"]}," As Medium creatures, Kel Dor have no special bonuses or penalties due to their size."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Speed:"]}," Kel Dor have a base speed of 6 squares."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Keen Force Sense:"]}," Kel Dor may choose to reroll any ",{"tag":"a","children":["Use the Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_the_Force","referenceId":"reference:74883d1dd46b87fe"}," check made to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Search Your Feelings"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Search_Your_Feelings"}," or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Sense Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sense_Force"},", keeping the better of the two results."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Low-Light Vision:"]}," Kel Dor ignore ",{"tag":"a","children":["Concealment"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Concealment"}," (but not ",{"tag":"a","children":["Total Concealment"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Total_Concealment"},") from darkness."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Special Equipment:"]}," Kel Dor suffer limitations outside their native atmosphere. Without protective goggles, a Kel Dor is considered ",{"tag":"a","children":["Blind"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Blind"},". Without an Antiox Breath Mask, a Kel Dor begins to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Suffocate"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Suffocate"},". A replacement mask costs 2,000 credits (500 on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dorin"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dorin","referenceId":"reference:4331a79784e79b6d"},"), and a year's supply of filters costs 200 credits (50 on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dorin"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dorin","referenceId":"reference:4331a79784e79b6d"},"). Kel Dor characters begin play with these items at no cost.\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":["An Antiox Breath Mask is poisonous to other ",{"tag":"a","children":["Species"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Species","referenceId":"reference:56205e12c20fb568"},"."]}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Automatic Languages:"]}," All Kel Dor can speak, read, and write both Basic and Kel Dor."]}]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Kel Dor Species Feats"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Rebellion Era Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Rebellion_Era_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Kel Dor characters have access to the following ",{"tag":"a","children":["Species Feats"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Species_Feats"},". No Species Feats are considered Bonus Feats for any ",{"tag":"a","children":["Heroic Class"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Heroic_Class"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"table","children":["\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["SPECIES FEAT\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["BENEFITS\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Justice Seeker"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Justice_Seeker","referenceId":"reference:8cedaac95ce6577a"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Gain a bonus to damage rolls against those who harm your allies.\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Read the Winds"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Read_the_Winds","referenceId":"reference:185ed317e6d38359"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Detect hidden enemies within 10 squares of you.\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Scion of Dorin"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scion_of_Dorin","referenceId":"reference:a80662b892010958"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Gain a bonus to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"}," against ",{"tag":"a","children":["Natural"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Natural"}," Hazards.\n"]}]}]}]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
